## Embroidery and surface work

| Term | What it is | Typical look |
|---|---|---|
| Zari | Metallic thread (gold or silver tone) used in weaving and embroidery | Shine and borders |
| Zardozi | Heavy hand embroidery with metallic thread, beads and sequins | Rich, raised bridal work |
| Gota patti | Folded metallic ribbon stitched onto fabric (Rajasthan) | Light, bright festive work |
| Resham | Embroidery with silk or silk-like thread | Colourful, soft motifs |
| Sequin work | Small shiny discs stitched on | Sparkle for evening wear |
| Mirror work | Small mirrors stitched with embroidery around them | Folk and festive look |
| Thread embroidery | Embroidery with plain thread | Light, comfortable daywear |
| Cutwork | Fabric cut away and edges finished with stitching | Open, lace-like patterns |
| Chikankari | Fine hand embroidery, traditionally white on white (Lucknow) | Delicate, minimal |
| Phulkari | Bright floral and geometric embroidery (Punjab) | Bold, joyful |
| Bandhani | Tie-dye technique creating small dots (Gujarat, Rajasthan) | Dotted patterns |
| Block print | Hand printing with carved wooden blocks | Repeating handmade prints |

